Open Vanilla / Open Vanilla 0021 — open sign-up, and the sign-in handoff only on the same network.

* DISCORD_OPEN_SIGNUP=1: anyone who signs in with Discord is let in without a wave role, and joins
  the Discord server already holding the sign-in role (Adventurer), so the server's gate bot sees a
  player with a realm account from the first moment and never stops them. Without it, a brand-new
  player was added to the server with no roles and then told "You're on the waitlist".
* Security fix for 0018's handoff ("Finish signing in on the page showing 4821?"): it is only offered
  when the browser Discord opened is on the same network (IPv4 /24, IPv6 /64) as the page that
  started. Someone who opened a sign-in page and sent its Discord link to a victim, asking them to
  confirm "the code", can no longer be signed in as the victim. The starting page's network is kept
  when /login, /auth/discord/start or the waiting page's status poll first sees it
  (migrations/0019_handoff_network.sql). Other browsers simply finish signing in where they are.
* tests/discord.rs: the start cookies are found by name (0018 added a second cookie); a new test for
  a brand-new Discord user with open sign-up. tests/signin.rs: requests carry a client address; new
  tests for the cross-network case and the network comparison.

